Fillets: two roundings that consume a face whose edges are all rounded
meet on one contact edge where their contacts end inside the face
(mitcad#1500).

A rib 2 wide with its four top edges rounded (or bevelled) by 1: the end
edges' contacts on the top face are cut to one point at the ridge by the
corners at both their ends (1652), and the long edges' contacts lie along
each other on the ridge, ending at those points, inside the face. 0950
joins such contacts only where they end on an edge of the face, so each
long blend kept its own contact edge and the top face was left as a face
of no area between the two edges along the ridge.

- joinEndsAlongContacts (0950): the ends of two such contacts inside the
  face (on no arc) are joined too, when every edge of the face is an edge
  of a stripe's spine (allEdgesRounded): the points are made one, and with
  both ends one the contacts are one edge, A's. With no edge of the face
  left for its contacts to end on, the face's edges are cut at their
  vertices, leaving the face on both sides, and the builder drops it.

